NAME
       vulnlookup - search the range's vulnerability notes (Cyber Range)

SYNOPSIS
       vulnlookup WORD...
       vulnlookup -x NUMBER

DESCRIPTION
       When a scan shows which program and version a server runs (nmap -sV, a
       Server header, a page footer), the next step is to look up what is known
       about that version. vulnlookup searches a small list of notes about the
       range's own products, which are all made up, and shows each note's
       number and title. -x NUMBER shows the whole note: what goes wrong, how
       to check it, and how the vendor fixed it.

       A version without notes isn't proof that it is safe, and a note isn't
       proof that a server is open to it: always check.

EXAMPLES
       vulnlookup acmecms
       vulnlookup -x 1

SEE ALSO
       nmap(1), curl(1), webscan(1)
